  "baseline_identity": "HEAD e69f2377 plus accepted dirty UR1c1 product and verifier deltas. Supplement b836c121 is historical pre-UR1c2 subject; do not demand new whole-tree equality. Capture new exact subject after C2 edits.",
  "frozen_scope": [
    "UR1c2 only: committed CompactStroke v4 GPU consumers in ordinary cooperative canonical and full transient/Direct paths. Reuse the existing renderer-owned PreparedGeometryCache and SourceRetentionPool; do not create another compiled-body/document owner.",
    "Separate ready lookup from build-capable admission. A new ordinary leaf must not call synchronous full-history get/build on a miss. First-use body preparation is resumable within the existing Render owner work allowance; in-flight jobs share immutable source identity and remain byte-budgeted.",
    "Ready bodies feed the actual canonical CompactStrokeRasterJob and real Direct/isolated material leaves, including the existing v4 damage-miss branch. Cache pixel hits skip geometry/coverage; geometry hits preserve exact original device grid, transform, masks, material and z-order.",
    "CPU geometry, distances/support and checkpoints can share across equal copies, transforms and mask-only changes. Changed config/seed/knot/type forks under UR1c1 complete equality/strong ownership rules. Source first-admission validation stays truthful; no digest/ObjectId shortcuts.",
    "New source-proportional compile/support/distance/path/group initialization is stepped. Charge every new body-build/replay operation to the existing allowance shared across the frame, not a fresh allowance per object/helper. Existing32knot compiler quanta remain the per-advance source bound; checkpoint blocks may remain256 but are assembled/replayed in bounded advances as needed.",
    "Exact compiled paths and bounded source-bound checkpoint replay are valid existing representations. Count unique full-body builds, cold admission comparisons/scans and visible checkpoint replay separately. Do not claim zero warm compilation when bounded checkpoint replay is used.",
    "Pending retains progress/source leases and does not publish partial current output or issue canonical receipts. Use existing preparation/dirty/retry seams; do readiness work before mutating the final provider target. Reject stale/unsupported/structurally impossible requests distinctly. Keep valid world body work across camera demand changes without reusing stale device pixels.",
    "Owner-thread only, same32/96MiB/maxEntry/maxEntries/preparation settings, same UR1b actual target and strict supported-GPU policy. No threads, SDK public API/ABI/version, Brush/Scene/History/Operation/input or UR2 change. Existing ready navigation/retained-ink consumers and private standalone compatibility callers continue to work; an in-progress C2 job cannot be synchronously drained by a compatibility caller.",
    "Explicit Raster/legacy/range/unsupported algorithms remain their existing declared compatibility paths. Do not feed the independent null-cache/null-prepared reference from the candidate prepared service. No wholeUR1,all-GPU,P34 or performanceSLO claim."
  ]
